{"operations":[{"content":"\"\"\"money: cent rounding for ledgers.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef round_cents(amount):\n    \"\"\"Round a decimal amount to cents, halves away from zero.\"\"\"\n    # Multiply by 100 to shift cents to integer domain\n    shifted = amount * 100\n    # Determine sign for rounding direction\n    sign = 1 if shifted >= 0 else -1\n    # Add 0.5 with sign to shift halves away from zero\n    shifted_rounded = int(shifted + sign * 0.5)\n    # Return back to decimal with two decimals\n    return shifted_rounded / 100\n","expected_sha256":"fa816984cb1f791630c850f452d214933dceee46a979c2276da8800a2c0570db","kind":"modify","path":"src/money.py"}],"rationale":"Replaced the default round with manual rounding that rounds halves away from zero as required, preserving the public API and usage by ledger.total."}